(6611349, 986131, 30364, '<td valign="top">That''s fun, and a good, interesting, ''breathing'' picture <strike>in spite of</strike> because of its photographic informality.  A very fine example of when it''s a good idea to forget about ticking all the boxes, and just enjoy the moment together.  Which makes it just right for a real rather than idealised family memory.  Thank you.  Do please accept a 9 and an Order of the Thumb: <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'That''s fun, and a good, interesting, ''breathing'' picture in spite of because of its photographic informality.  A very fine example of when it''s a good idea to forget about ticking all the boxes, and just enjoy the moment together.  Which makes it just right for a real rather than idealised family memory.  Thank you.  Do please accept a 9 and an Order of the Thumb: ', '2011-12-05 17:00:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6611350, 985444, 30364, '<td valign="top">Beautifully balanced between a family record and a family hug.  It has many lovely fine details (including your own clever disappearance), but it''s the overall feeling of mutual affection - you for them and they for you, and for each other - that makes this such a lovely family picture.  Thank you. A 10 from me (one point per person), and the alarming Order of the Thumb:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Beautifully balanced between a family record and a family hug.  It has many lovely fine details (including your own clever disappearance), but it''s the overall feeling of mutual affection - you for them and they for you, and for each other - that makes this such a lovely family picture.  Thank you. A 10 from me (one point per person), and the alarming Order of the Thumb:', '2011-12-05 17:01:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6611358, 985974, 30364, '<td valign="top">A lovely, literally charming photograph.  It manages to be both a smile-inducing family ''snap'' and a really superb photograph at the same time.  That''s because it just <i>looks</i> like the former while actually being the latter.  I think it''s comfortably the best and most interesting picture in the challenge.  Thoughtful, unusual, clever, photographically irreverent and perfectly executed - it''s not often someone at DPC produces a picture with this kind of genuine substance and durability, that appears so modest at first glance (it''s more usually the reverse).  10 and thank you.  Plus the best-avoided Order of the Thumb:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'A lovely, literally charming photograph.  It manages to be both a smile-inducing family ''snap'' and a really superb photograph at the same time.  That''s because it just looks like the former while actually being the latter.  I think it''s comfortably the best and most interesting picture in the challenge.  Thoughtful, unusual, clever, photographically irreverent and perfectly executed - it''s not often someone at DPC produces a picture with this kind of genuine substance and durability, that appears so modest at first glance (it''s more usually the reverse).  10 and thank you.  Plus the best-avoided Order of the Thumb:', '2011-12-05 17:09:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6611427, 985680, 69446, '<td valign="top">A nice photo... personally I''d have liked to see greater depth of field to keep both subjects in focus. The dog is a little blurred.</td>', 'A nice photo... personally I''d have liked to see greater depth of field to keep both subjects in focus. The dog is a little blurred.', '2011-12-05 18:18:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6611431, 985974, 69446, '<td valign="top">The strong sunlight makes this image quite contrasty... lighting would be better early or late in the day. The girl is a bit overexposed and out of focus.</td>', 'The strong sunlight makes this image quite contrasty... lighting would be better early or late in the day. The girl is a bit overexposed and out of focus.', '2011-12-05 18:23:11.000000', NULL, 1),
